
test/Warn/CompileToInstanceInconsistent.agda:11.3-9: warning: -W[no]CustomBackendWarning
agda2hs:
  The instance iEqVec is annotated with a `to` pragma targeting iEqList,
    but the two instances do not compile to the same Haskell declaration:
  compiled instance iEqVec:
    instance (Eq a) => Eq ([a]) where
        (==) = eqList
          where
            eqList :: [a] -> [a] -> Bool
            eqList [] [] = True
            eqList (x : xs) (y : ys) = x == y || eqList xs ys
  compiled instance iEqList:
    instance (Eq a) => Eq ([a]) where
        (==) = eqList
          where
            eqList :: [a] -> [a] -> Bool
            eqList [] [] = True
            eqList (x : xs) (y : ys) = x == y && eqList xs ys
            eqList _ _ = False
